Falsifies `memory_regions::proofs::a_return_keeps_every_run_inside_its_parents_spent_part`.

The defect: the reclaim after a return drops the floor of the parent's own retypes and lowers the
watermark to where its highest live child ends. It reads as the whole of the reclaim, since a hole
is what the pass exists to close, and the pages the parent retyped for itself sit below no child.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(s.retyped_to <= s.watermark, "retyped past the watermark")`,
for a child whose own retypes reach past its last live grandchild.

--- a/crates/memory_regions/src/watermark.rs
+++ b/crates/memory_regions/src/watermark.rs
@@ -65,5 +65,5 @@
     if !quiescent {
         return watermark;
     }
-    retyped_to.max(live_to).min(watermark)
+    live_to.min(watermark)
 }
